# VVA — LangGraph service configuration (template).
#
# Copy to `.env` NEXT TO THIS FILE and fill in the secrets:
#     cp agenticRAG/.env.example agenticRAG/.env
#
# This directory is the canonical location. `agenticRAG/langgraph_agents/shared/env.py`
# is the only loader in the service; it reads `agenticRAG/.env`, still accepts the
# legacy `agenticRAG/agentic_rag_gemini/.env` with a warning, and warns when it finds
# neither.
#
# Real environment variables ALWAYS win over this file (`override=False`), so a
# container or systemd unit passing its own configuration is never silently
# overridden by a stray file on the image.
#
# Everything below is optional unless marked REQUIRED — the defaults shown are what
# the code uses when the variable is absent.


# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWO credentials, on purpose. Since migration 007 the user tables carry
# row-level security, and PostgreSQL exempts a table's OWNER from its own
# policies — so an application connecting as the owner would have RLS enabled,
# listed by \d+, and completely inert.
#
#   VVA_PG_DSN        what the application connects as: `eca_user`, least
#                     privilege, policies apply to it
#   VVA_PG_DSN_OWNER  migrations only. Alembic reads this first (alembic/env.py)
#                     because DDL needs the owner. Never give it to the app.
#
# Development uses the same application role as production, deliberately: a
# query that forgets its user scope then fails on the developer's machine
# instead of after deploy. To inspect all rows while debugging, export the owner
# DSN as VVA_PG_DSN for that one shell.
#
# Without either, the service falls back to the local Docker container
# (postgresql://vva:vva_dev@localhost:5433/vva) and logs a warning saying so.
# That fallback used to be silent, which is how the app and Alembic ended up on
# two different databases.
#
# Neon endpoint choice: the DIRECT hostname is the default here. The CRUD Lambda
# uses the `-pooler` one (SSM /vva/neon/dsn-pooler) because ephemeral containers
# are what PgBouncer exists to absorb — measured 18-08, prepared statements do
# survive Neon's pooler, so the old "direct only" rule does not apply to it.
VVA_PG_DSN=postgresql://eca_user:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
VVA_PG_DSN_OWNER=postgresql://owner:password@host.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require
# Accepted as an alias for VVA_PG_DSN, for shells that already export it.
# POSTGRES_DSN=

# Read the DSN from an SSM SecureString instead, by name. Used on Lambda, where
# a connection string in an environment variable would sit in plaintext in the
# CloudFormation template. Ranks below the variables above.
# VVA_PG_DSN_PARAM=/vva/neon/dsn-pooler

# Per-query timing counters, exposed at /debug/pgstats. Off unless set to 1.
# VVA_PG_STATS=0


# ── LLM providers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DeepSeek is the primary provider; Gemini is the fallback when its circuit
# breaker opens. Both keys are secrets — never commit a filled-in copy.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# Comma-separated; the client rotates across them on quota errors.
GEMINI_API_KEYS=

# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL_FAST=deepseek-chat
# LLM_MODEL=

# Include a real LLM round-trip in /health/detailed. Off by default: it costs a
# call on every probe, and the circuit breaker already reports provider trouble.
# LLM_HEALTHCHECK=0


# ── Dependent services ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vietnamese TTS (CPU). Optional dependency: if it is down the assistant still
# answers, just without speech, and /health/detailed reports "degraded" on a 200.
# VIENEU_URL=http://localhost:5000

# Self-hosted web search, used as the retrieval fallback. Also optional.
# SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:6666

# Motion synthesis. Host/port variants are used when the full URL is not given.
# DART_URL=http://localhost:5001
# TTS_URL=http://localhost:5000
# AGENTIC_RAG_URL=http://localhost:8000

# The host/port halves, for when you want to move one service without rewriting
# a whole URL. Each *_URL above wins over its host/port pair.
# AGENTIC_RAG_HOST=localhost      AGENTIC_RAG_PORT=8000
# DART_HOST=localhost             DART_PORT=5001
# TTS_HOST=localhost              TTS_PORT=5000


# ── Main API tuning (core/config/settings.py) ────────────────────────────────
# Undocumented until 19-08. Everything here has a working default, which is why
# nobody noticed — but a default you cannot discover is one you cannot change.
# MAIN_API_PORT=8080
# MAIN_API_ASYNC_ENRICHMENT=true    # enrich in the background after responding
# MAIN_API_INCLUDE_DEBUG=true       # include debug blocks in responses
# MOTION_DEFAULT_DURATION_SECONDS=5.33
# DOWNSTREAM_TIMEOUT=90.0           # calls out to DART / TTS / agentic-rag
# DOWNSTREAM_SESSION_TIMEOUT=15.0   # per-session cap within that

# Rollout flags. All default OFF — turning one on enables an unfinished path.
# FEATURE_HYBRID_RETRIEVAL=false
# FEATURE_MOTION_TRANSLATOR=false
# FEATURE_EARLY_ASYNC_MOTION=false
# FEATURE_DART_FAST_DRAFT=false

# Latency budgets in milliseconds — reporting thresholds, not enforced timeouts.
# SLA_COMMON_QNA_MS=4000
# SLA_KNOWN_MOTION_MS=8000
# SLA_NOVEL_MOTION_MS=15000

# Concurrency caps (core/resource_guard.py).
# AGENTIC_MAX_TOOL_CONCURRENCY=
# AGENTIC_EMBEDDING_CACHE_SIZE=


# ── API server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated CORS allow-list. Keep the frontend origins only.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# MAIN_API_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Cognito JWT verification. REQUIRED — the API takes identity only from a
# verified token, and refuses to start without a pool to verify against. There is
# no flag that relaxes this; dev and production are separated by WHICH POOL they
# trust, not by whether they check.
#
# For development, point these at your own sandbox pool from `npx ampx sandbox`
# (ECA_UI/frontend/amplify). A token minted there is rejected by production
# because the issuer differs — which is exactly the separation we want.
#
# Mint a token for curl/Postman with scripts/dev_token.ps1.
#
# AUTH_PROVIDER is not listed as a knob because it has exactly one valid value.
# A Clerk branch was removed on 19-08 — its frontend half had already been
# deleted, so the backend could verify tokens the UI had no way to obtain. The
# variable still exists only so that a stale AUTH_PROVIDER=clerk in someone's
# environment raises at startup instead of being quietly ignored.
COGNITO_REGION=
COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=
COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID=

# Dev user for scripts/dev_token.ps1 (sandbox pool only — never a real account).
# VVA_DEV_USERNAME=dev@local
# VVA_DEV_PASSWORD=


# ── Billing sandbox (optional, real transactions are disabled in code) ───────
# Leave false to disable every Stripe write endpoint. Turn it on only after all
# three sandbox values below are configured. Live keys are rejected even when
# this flag is true. Billing integrates directly with Stripe.
BILLING_SANDBOX_ENABLED=false
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_TEST_PRICE_ID=price_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Stripe Checkout/Portal return destination. Without it, local development uses
# the request Origin only for localhost/127.0.0.1 and otherwise falls back here.
# FRONTEND_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173


# ── Embeddings ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# intfloat/multilingual-e5-small, loaded from the local HuggingFace cache. Set to 1
# only on a machine allowed to download it the first time; leaving it on means a
# network hiccup turns into a start-up failure.
# EMBEDDING_ALLOW_DOWNLOAD=0


# ── Character assets (S3 / CloudFront) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Read by scripts/upload_characters_to_s3.py ONLY — the FastAPI service never
# talks to S3. The catalog endpoints live in the vva-characters Lambda
# (infra/lambda/characters), and the service reads characters.persona straight
# from Postgres at startup.
#
# The script authenticates through the ordinary boto3 chain (AWS_PROFILE, or the
# standard AWS_* variables), so nothing new belongs here. Both values come from
# VvaAssetStack outputs and are passed as flags rather than read from the
# environment, to keep "which bucket did I seed?" visible in shell history:
#
#   python scripts/upload_characters_to_s3.py \
#       --bucket   <AssetBucketName> \
#       --cdn      https://<AssetBaseUrl>
#
# The Lambda gets its own connection string from SSM (/vva/neon/dsn, a
# SecureString created out of band), NOT from this file — a Lambda outside the
# VPC reads SSM over the ordinary internet path, so no VPC endpoint is involved.


# ── Docker ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by docker-compose.langgraph.yml (searxng service), not by the Python
# service. It lives here because a second .env file at the repo root, holding one
# variable, was one more thing to hand a new teammate and one more thing to
# forget. Any non-empty random string works; searxng uses it to sign sessions.
SEARXNG_SECRET_KEY=

# ── Logging / tracing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# LOG_FILE=
# AGENTIC_TRACE=0
